{"name":"Panda","hex":"#544f3a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Panda","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A South Asian surname."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Panda"}],"entries":[{"title":"Giant panda","blocks":[{"text":"The giant panda, also known as the panda bear or simply panda, is a bear species endemic to China. It is characterised by its white coat with black patches around the eyes, ears, legs and shoulders. Its body is rotund; adult individuals weigh 100 to 115 kg and are typically 1.2 to 1.9 m long. It is sexually dimorphic, with males being typically 10–20% larger than females. A thumb is visible on its forepaw, which helps in holding bamboo in place for feeding. It has large molar teeth and expanded temporal fossae to meet its dietary requirements. It can digest starch and is mostly herbivorous with a diet consisting almost entirely of bamboo and bamboo shoots."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Grosser_Panda.JPG/330px-Grosser_Panda.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Giant_panda","wikidata":"Q33602"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Qinling_panda.jpg/500px-Qinling_panda.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Qinling_panda.jpg/500px-Qinling_panda.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Qinling panda has a light brown-and-white pattern.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AQuinlingpandabearr.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Giant_panda_on_a_white_background.png/500px-Giant_panda_on_a_white_background.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Giant_panda_on